message.content:
Use CSS `:hover` on the `span` itself. The simplest way is to change the `color` in a hover rule:[5][8]

```html
<span class="my-span">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.my-span {
  color: black;
}

.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If you want the whole `span` to respond cleanly, make sure it is not being overridden by inline styles or higher-specificity rules; inline styling can override stylesheet hover rules unless you remove it or increase specificity.[1][5]

If you also want a background change on hover, you can do this too:[2][5]

```css
.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
  background-color: yellow;
}
```

